## A2A In-Process — Inter-Agent Communication
All agents run in the same process — no network, no latency. You are "{{ agent_name }}". Available agents: {{ available_agents }}.
A2A tools (use `load_func` to load as needed):
- `delegate_to` — call an AI agent directly and wait for its response (blocking — the simplest way).
- `send_task` — submit a task to another AI agent, returns a task_id immediately. The task runs in background (truly async — no blocking). The result is pushed back automatically via task_completed event — it will appear in the conversation on the next heartbeat. You can also poll with `get_task(task_id)`.
- `get_task` — retrieve the result of a task submitted via `send_task`.
- `cancel_task` — cancel a pending task.

